## 5. Environment and infrastructure

### ENV-1 · CI has never been observed green · OPEN
The remote exists and `main`, `staging` and both tags are pushed, so the
blocking half of this is gone. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` is valid YAML with
2 jobs and 17 steps, but validity is not the same as passing and no run has
been watched.

- Needed: confirm the first run is green and fix whatever it finds.
- Until then every "all gates pass" claim rests on local runs only.

### ENV-2 · Vercel CLI not installed · OPEN
`npm i -g vercel` then `vercel login && vercel link`. README.md and
DEVELOPMENT.md both document `npm run env:pull`, which cannot work yet.

### ENV-3 · MCP servers unavailable · OPEN
- `vercel` and `supabase` need OAuth, which cannot run in a non-interactive
  session — authorise via claude.ai connector settings or `/mcp`.
- `github` fails with "Authorization header is badly formatted" — a
  connection fault, not a missing capability.

### ENV-4 · Git identity may misattribute commits · OPEN · low
Commits are authored as `jacob.frusher@cil-uk.co.uk`, which differs from the
account email on this session. If GitHub uses the other address the history
will not attribute. Cheap to fix now, annoying later.

### ENV-5 · Branch protection not configured · OPEN
DEVELOPMENT.md §5.6 specifies protecting `main` and `staging`. Until set, the
branching model is a convention rather than a rule.


