## 6. Scope and documentation drift

### DOC-1 · `/dev/theme` ships to production · OPEN · low
The design-system reference page is a real route in the production bundle.
Either gate it behind `NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV !== 'production'` or accept it
deliberately and say so in CLAUDE.md.

### DOC-2 · CLAUDE.md §2.2 directory map is aspirational · OPEN
Less wrong than it was: `AppShell`, `CycleBar`, `SqlConsole` and the whole
`components/preview/` and `components/imposition/` trees now exist.

Still listed and still absent: `CanvasRulers`, `Guides` (both INC-1/INC-2),
`RecordSourcePanel`, `InspectorPanel`, `TypographyPanel`. The map also omits
components that do exist — `ImageImport`, `TutorialPanel`, `DiagnosticsPanel`,
`ResizeHandle`, `components/brand/`.

Fine as a target, misleading as a map — mark which parts are built.

### DOC-3 · `components/ui/` is not "retuned Shadcn" · OPEN · low
CLAUDE.md §4.5 describes retuning Shadcn primitives. No Shadcn is installed:
`Button` and `Modal` are hand-written, and the dialog uses native `<dialog>`.
That was a deliberate call recorded in §7, but §4.5 still reads as though a
component library is in use.

### DOC-4 · `fixtures/` images are unreferenced masters · OPEN · low
Ten images committed in `f48735b`. Six are now the brand artwork, copied into
`public/brand/` and served from there; the wordmark and favicon were redrawn
as SVG rather than used directly. Nothing imports `fixtures/` itself.

Decide: keep as the source masters the served copies derive from — and say so
in a short note — or drop them, since they are only recoverable from history
afterwards.

### DOC-5 · `useDataStore` re-exports `isOk` · OPEN · trivial
A leftover convenience export from a store module. Import from `@/lib/result`
and remove.

---

## 7. Decisions — considered and declined

Recorded so they are not rediscovered as problems. Each was considered and
declined on the merits — they are choices, not debt.

### Deliberate scope limits

- **INC-12 · Save always downloads a new file.** The File System Access API
  could overwrite the opened file, but it is Chromium-only and cannot be
  driven from a test. Revisit if repeated saving becomes annoying in practice.
- **INC-17 · No text shaping.** `measureText` sums advance widths from
  `font.layout()`, which covers Latin with kerning — the scope CLAUDE.md §8
  sets for v1. Ligatures, contextual alternates and complex scripts will
  measure and render incorrectly. Fixing it means HarfBuzz.
- **INC-25 · Export cancellation is per-sheet.** `shouldCancel` is checked
  between sheets; a sheet takes tens of milliseconds, so the delay is
  imperceptible. Finer granularity means threading a signal through every draw
  call.
- **INC-28 · SQL console highlighting has no parser.** Token-level colouring
  over a transparent textarea, so a keyword inside an unterminated string
  still colours. The alternative is CodeMirror 6 and its dependency tree for
  bracket matching and completion the console does not need. Revisit only if
  people start writing long queries in it.
- **INC-29 · Templates are TypeScript, not `.toke` files.** A `.toke` carries a
  complete SQLite file, so shipping one needs a build step running sql.js to
  produce a binary that drifts whenever the schema changes. Declaring the
  design in `engine/templates/templates.ts` and importing the roster through
  the normal CSV path is typechecked and exercises the real user path.
- **INC-36 · Mascot artwork is raster.** Six ~110KB PNGs at ~320px, rendered at
  48–112px. The brace mark IS vector. Redraw the character only if it ever
  needs to be large.
- **ENV-6 · Caveman statusline badge.** A local tooling preference, not a
  property of this project.

### Library and platform choices

- **`pdf-lib` is unmaintained** (1.17.1, ~4 years old). Deliberate: used as a
  low-level writer under our own renderer. CLAUDE.md §7.
- **No `@tanstack/react-table`.** Dropped after building the grid; runtime
  schema introspection plus sort earned nothing from a headless table model.
- **Native `<dialog>` over a modal library.** `showModal()` already provides
  focus trap, Escape, `aria-modal` and inert background.
- **Next auto-appends a block to CLAUDE.md** on `next dev`. Committed
  deliberately; removing it only recreates the diff.
- **`ink-disabled` fails AA contrast on purpose** (2.93:1). WCAG exempts
  disabled controls, and the contrast test asserts it stays below threshold so
  nobody "fixes" it into looking enabled.
- **RGB PDF output, not CMYK.** No ICC embedding is achievable client-side.
  CLAUDE.md §9.
